From 88399a8bede664b083a72ad2fe6774dfff660df6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Agent <claude-agent@invalid>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:11:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Make the focused image-colour regressions build and tear down
 cleanly

The first build and run of TestWebCoreImageColour found four fixture
defects; no shipping code changes:

- pass ICC bytes as explicit const spans, and spell the draw rectangle as
  a FloatRect; both calls are ambiguous in 2.52.6
- build the LUT-only P3 test profile with a 16-bit CLUT. lutAtoBType
  serialises only 8/16-bit CLUTs, so the float CLUT made
  cmsSaveProfileToMem fail. The u1Fixed15 table keeps the same XYZ
- release the thread-local Skia context in SkiaWorkingTextureTest's
  TearDown with its own GL context current. Otherwise GrDirectContext
  freed its GL objects from TLS destructors at exit with no context
  current, and libepoxy aborted. 2.52.6's defaulted ~SkiaGLContext is the
  upstream shutdown-ordering issue fixed by WebKit e0b1fddaa468 (bug
  305909); that 13-file change is outside this series

Agent-Model: claude-opus-5-5
Agent-Session: 01BCWL9zQ3AH5jz3cWrpdXCg
